{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 23 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D8"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the carboplatin shortage on 2023-04-28 and it has remained current for 42 months as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E31", "D12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Accord Healthcare product on the shortage list uses Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited as a registered manufacturing plant.",
      "cites": ["E20", "E21"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1191818 of Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited ended 2022-12-02 and was classified OAI, with the classification letter dated 2023-04-05.",
      "cites": ["E16"]
    },
    {
      "text": "That OAI classification letter came 23 days before FDA posted the shortage on 2023-04-28.",
      "cites": ["D8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA subsequently issued an import alert 66-40 listing Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited on 2023-06-01 and a Warning Letter on 2023-07-28.",
      "cites": ["E18", "E17"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our Corvale East site holds two carboplatin products: Teva (NDC 00703423901) manufactured by PHARMACHEMIE BV and Apotex (NDC 60505628201) manufactured by Teyro Labs Private Limited.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E9", "E2", "E11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑ranked best option is to transfer 26 units from Corvale East to Corvale Lakeside, which would give Corvale Lakeside 14 days on hand while Corvale East retains two weeks of supply.",
      "cites": ["D9"]
    }
  ]
}
